# Bulletproof Components

Colocate components, styles, and state as close as possible to where they are used.

## Structure

- Shared UI lives in `src/components` (shadcn/ui + app wrappers). Feature UI lives in `src/features/<domain>/components`.
- One component, one responsibility. If a piece of UI is a unit, extract it to its own file.
- Do not nest `renderFoo()` functions inside a component. Extract `<Foo />`.
- Prefer composition (`children`, slots) over a long props list. If a component takes too many props, split it.
- Wrap third-party and shadcn primitives in `src/components/ui` so call sites do not depend on the library directly.

```tsx
// ❌ nested render helpers
function Page() {
  function renderList() { return <ul>...</ul> }
  return <div>{renderList()}</div>
}

// ✅ extracted unit
function ItemList() { return <ul>...</ul> }
function Page() { return <div><ItemList /></div> }
```

## Styling

- Tailwind only, via `cn`. No ad hoc CSS-in-JS.
- Identify repetition before adding a shared primitive. Wrong abstractions are worse than duplication.
- Keep interactive pieces accessible (label, `type`, keyboard). This app is mobile first.
